  "body": "#8528 added the \"has been scrolled by the user\" boolean, to support speccing scroll restoration. It's currently set via action-at-a-distance:\r\n\r\n> If the user scrolls the document, the user agent must set that document's <span>has been scrolled by the user</span> to true.\r\n\r\nInstead, we could consider setting it as part of the spec that specifies the rest of the scrolling behavior. Namely, https://w3c.github.io/csswg-drafts/cssom-view/#document-pending-scroll-event-targets has\r\n\r\n> Whenever a [viewport](https://w3c.github.io/csswg-drafts/css2/#viewport%E2%91%A0) gets scrolled (whether in response to user interaction or by an API), the user agent must run these steps:\r\n\r\nWe could make that a bit more explicit, and have it set the Document's value.",
